faqs:
- q: Do you do long-distance removals for older people?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK, including long-distance moves closer to children or grandchildren.
- q: Can I arrange a long-distance move for a parent from far away?
  a: Yes. Moves are often arranged by adult children on a parent&rsquo;s behalf. You can be involved by phone or video, and your coordinator keeps you updated throughout.
- q: How do you manage a move if you are not nearby?
  a: One coordinator manages the move from the first conversation to settling in, in person where it matters and remotely in between. Where possible, viewings and key moving-day tasks are scheduled together.
- q: How much does a long-distance removal cost?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and an insured removal. Silver Comfort at {silver} adds sorting and declutter help, a deep clean and unpacking. The final price depends on the size of the property and the support you need, and is confirmed in writing before you book.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: What if the sale and the move-in dates do not match?
  a: Dates often shift. Gold Prestige includes up to six weeks of storage to bridge the gap, and storage can be discussed for other packages. See <a href="/storage-during-your-move/">storage between house moves</a>.
- q: Do you move people to and from the Midlands cities?
  a: Yes. See our guide to <a href="/blog/removals-leicester-coventry-oxford-cambridge-peterborough-longer-moves/">longer moves to Leicester, Coventry, Oxford, Cambridge and Peterborough</a>.
- q: Who looks after my parent&rsquo;s belongings on the day?
  a: Our own DBS-checked team, not outsourced. See our <a href="/trust-and-safeguarding/">trust and safeguarding page</a>.
